  "functional_objectives": [
    "THE CLI SHALL provide a validate command that checks JSONL syntax, required fields, and severity levels.",
    "WHEN the user invokes the summarize command with valid input, THE CLI SHALL group events by case_id and produce a deterministic timeline for each case.",
    "WHEN the user invokes the explain command with --event-id EVENT_ID, THE CLI SHALL locate the event whose event_id equals EVENT_ID and display its local context within the corresponding case timeline.",
    "WHEN the user invokes the schema command, THE CLI SHALL display the minimum expected event contract.",
    "WHERE a command supports event filtering, THE CLI SHALL accept the --case-id, --actor, --min-severity, and --tag filters when they are applicable to that command.",
    "WHERE --redact is supplied, THE CLI SHALL mask email addresses, long tokens, and long hexadecimal identifiers in human-readable output.",
    "WHEN two executions receive identical input content and identical arguments, THE CLI SHALL produce identical output.",
    "WHEN the input operand equals '-', THE CLI SHALL read JSONL event records from stdin instead of opening a local input file.",
    "WHEN a successful command is invoked without --output, THE CLI SHALL emit its text report, JSON report, schema diagnostic, or event context to stdout.",
    "WHERE --output is supplied to a command that supports file output, THE CLI SHALL write the command result to the selected local output file.",
    "IF the CLI receives an invalid argument, unknown option, unknown subcommand, missing required input, unreadable path, or local read or write failure, THEN THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit a short user-readable error to stderr without traceback.",
    "WHEN top-level help is displayed, THE CLI SHALL identify the validate, summarize, explain, and schema commands.",
    "WHEN validate help is displayed, THE CLI SHALL include the fragments usage:, validate, and input.",
    "WHEN summarize help is displayed, THE CLI SHALL include the fragments usage:, summarize, input, --format, and --min-severity.",
    "WHEN explain help is displayed, THE CLI SHALL include the fragments usage:, explain, input, and --event-id.",
    "WHEN schema help is displayed, THE CLI SHALL include the fragments usage: and schema."
  ],
  "non_functional_constraints": [
    "THE CLI SHALL operate without network access.",
    "THE CLI SHALL require no mandatory external dependency beyond the Python standard library.",
    "WHEN any application module is imported, THE module SHALL perform no argument parsing, command execution, file read, stdin read, filesystem write, stream emission, network access, or subprocess execution.",
    "THE CLI SHALL sort events deterministically by normalized timestamp, then case_id, then event_id.",
    "WHEN an expected user-facing error occurs, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit a short readable message without a traceback.",
    "WHEN JSON output is produced, THE CLI SHALL serialize object keys in sorted order wherever the selected JSON representation permits it.",
    "THE CLI SHALL run on Windows and POSIX platforms.",
    "WHILE any command is executing, THE CLI SHALL NOT modify the input file.",
    "WHEN two executions receive identical input content and identical arguments, THE CLI SHALL produce equal exit codes, stdout content, stderr content, and output-file content.",
    "WHILE a successful command result is emitted, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit no unrelated banner, debug line, progress line, log line, advisory prose, or duplicate result.",
    "WHEN a command succeeds, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL return exit code 0 and emit nothing to stderr.",
    "WHEN bad CLI arguments are detected, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL return exit code 2, emit the applicable short error to stderr, and emit no command result to stdout."
  ],
  "architectural_objectives": [
    "THE generated architecture SHALL clearly separate the CLI surface, JSONL parsing, business validation, filtering, timeline construction, redaction, and rendering responsibilities.",
